          ],
          "content": "Curiosity | Textbook of Science | Grade 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.083,
            0.892,
            0.111,
            0.908
          ],
          "content": "30"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.483,
            0.101,
            0.628,
            0.124
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Summary"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.157,
            0.882,
            0.2
          ],
          "content": " We are surrounded by a large variety of plants and animals. Such variety of plants and animals is a part of biodiversity."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.206,
            0.883,
            0.248
          ],
          "content": " Plants and animals can be grouped on the basis of similarities and differences among them."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.254,
            0.883,
            0.296
          ],
          "content": " Plants have similarities and differences based on features associated with roots, stems, leaves, flowers, and so on."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.303,
            0.883,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": " The method of arranging things into groups based on their common features is called grouping."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.352,
            0.882,
            0.394
          ],
          "content": " Plants can be grouped into herbs, shrubs, and trees based on their heights, types of stem, and branching patterns."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.4,
            0.885,
            0.463
          ],
          "content": " Plants can also be grouped as dicotyledons (dicots) and monocotyledons (monocots) based on the number of cotyledons in their seeds."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.47,
            0.883,
            0.535
          ],
          "content": " Monocots generally exhibit parallel venation in their leaves and possess fibrous roots while dicots typically exhibit reticulate venation in their leaves and possess taproots."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.54,
            0.883,
            0.582
          ],
          "content": "basis for their grouping."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.588,
            0.883,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": " Biodiversity of different regions varies because of distinct environmental conditions."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.637,
            0.883,
            0.68
          ],
          "content": " The special features that enable plants and animals to survive in a particular region are called adaptations."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.686,
            0.845,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": " The place where plants and animals live is their habitat."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.713,
            0.883,
            0.755
          ],
          "content": " Based on their habitats, animals and plants can be grouped as terrestrial and aquatic."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.762,
            0.883,
            0.825
          ],
          "content": " Due to damage of their habitats, plants and animals lose their homes, food and other resources resulting in the loss of biodiversity."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.832,
            0.884,
            0.875
          ],
          "content": " We must protect biodiversity to ensure that our planet is full of life, helping plants and animals to survive and thrive."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.971,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
